  "description_html": "Diagram of the known material of the forefin of MOZ 5803, the holotype and only known specimen of the Bajocian Argentine ichthyosaur <i>Chacaicosaurus cayi</i>, as preserved, following Fernández (1994). The partial humerus and isolated phalanges were not found in articulation with the rest of the limb and are therefore not included here.\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ul><li><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Fernández, M. S. (1994). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://books.google.com/books?hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;id=Xeo9pTkWJHsC&amp;oi=fnd&amp;pg=PA291&amp;dq=Chacaicosaurus&amp;ots=3z4YEEfTfq&amp;sig=HFPw0c1Jop07nORpwECx_ecRFP8#v=onepage&amp;q&amp;f=false\">A new long-snouted ichthyosaur from the Early Bajocian of Neuquén Basin, Argentina</a>\". <i>Ameghiniana</i> <b>31</b> (3): 291–297.</cite></li></ul>",
